### Tenant south's own working set, created by a key with EXACTLY the rights `dispatcher-north` has.
### That is what makes 080-Tenancy a claim about tenancy: anything either dispatcher cannot see is
### not explainable by a difference in role, scope or rule.
# @name CreateSouthCustomer
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/customers
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherSouth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenant_id": "{{tenantSouth}}",
  "name": "Southern Foods",
  "tier": "standard",
  "email": "hello@southernfoods.test"
}

### `regions` is global, so the SAME region row serves both tenants — the contrast that makes
### "scoped" mean something rather than being the only behaviour on offer.
# @name CreateSouthWorkOrder
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherSouth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenant_id": "{{tenantSouth}}",
  "reference": "WO-5001",
  "title": "Chiller service",
  "status": "scheduled",
  "priority": 1,
  "quoted_price": 430.00,
  "is_emergency": false,
  "internal_notes": "Southern tenant only.",
  "access_code": "SOUTH-5001",
  "customer_id": "{{CreateSouthCustomer.response.body.$.id}}",
  "region_id": "{{RegionNorthId}}"
}

### Tenant south reads the shared reference data tenant north's admin created
# @name SouthReadsGlobalRegions
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/regions?limit=100&order=code.asc
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherSouth}}
